"Create a file named split_lines.sh in the current directory with exactly the following content (keep every character as given):\n\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# split_lines.sh: print every field of the first argument on its own line\nIFS=,\nread -r -a parts <<< \"$1\"\nfor p in \"${parts[@]}\"; do\n  echo \"[$p]\"\ndone\n"